The plug-in backend interface — a provenance boundary, recorded because it is
load-bearing (src/host/pluginbackend.h):

  The method list of the interface every hosted plug-in format implements is
  re-derived from the MIT-licensed function set in the author's own Haiku plug-in
  host, whose internal header declares the same operations as a flat list of
  extern "C" functions per format, dispatched on a format tag.

  It is NOT derived from that project's Linux sibling. That sibling has no licence
  file, states GPLv2 intent, and its VST2 backend includes a GPLv2 ABI header.
  NOTHING FROM THAT TREE MAY ENTER THIS INCLUDE GRAPH, and the comment recording
  this travels with the file rather than living only here.

  This is a case where two trees by the same author sit side by side under
  different terms, and the difference is easy to lose in a port. It is written
  down in both places for that reason.

